    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other files in that package are the base and helper). `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nTo make owner creation return `displayName` formatted as `\"LastName, FirstName\"`, I made two small, targeted changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the API response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a small `displayName(Owner)` default helper that formats the stored last/first names as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nThe formatting logic lives in the mapper (the API-representation layer, where the derived field belongs) as a single-purpose helper, and both the direct create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read reuse the same `toOwnerDto` path \u2014 no duplication. The domain `Owner`/`Person` entities are untouched, keeping persistence concerns separate from presentation.",
